Buildpacks
===========
1. A buildpack is a tool which converts an application source code to an executable container image.
2. There are many buildpacks available from different vendors based on common programming ecosystem like java, phython
3. Buildpacks can be grouped together to form a builder, which independently looks for the specific file in the code, based on
   its configuration and the decides whether to participate in the building the proccess or not.


How to do it
==============
1. Go to project pom.xml file > build section > configuration section
then enter below tags
   <image>
      <name>anandmohansinha(docker hub userId)/${project.artifactId} </name>
   </image>

2. click on project and run maven build> edit configuration pop up will open > in Goal section you have to enter
      spring-boot:build-image
